<BaseLayout title="Kona Token Trade · Backend Case Study" description="A public-safe case study of Nieb Hasan Neom's backend contributions to a blockchain-based token-trading platform." active="Work">
  <header class="case-header page-shell">
    <a class="back-link" href="/work">← Work & Research</a>
    <div class="case-kicker"><span class="eyebrow">COMPLETED BACKEND CASE STUDY</span><span class="schema-chip">PUBLIC-SAFE SCOPE</span></div>
    <h1>Kona Token Trade</h1>
    <p>Backend engineering across trade, user, wallet, and fee-management services, with focused contributions to reliable communication, response latency, and sensitive-operation security.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="case-facts page-shell" aria-label="Case study facts">
    <span><small>ROLE</small><strong>Software Engineer II</strong></span>
    <span><small>PERIOD</small><strong>Apr 2022 - Jun 2025</strong></span>
    <span><small>DOMAIN</small><strong>Token trading</strong></span>
    <span><small>EVIDENCE</small><strong>Reviewed résumé + owner approval</strong></span>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section page-shell">
    <div class="case-section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">CONTRIBUTION MAP</span><h2>Specific ownership, without claiming the whole platform.</h2><p>This diagram organizes the approved contribution areas. It is not a representation of Kona’s proprietary topology.</p></div>
    <div class="contribution-map" aria-label="Approved contribution areas">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Service domains</h3><p>Trade, user, wallet, and fee-management services.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Reliable communication</h3><p>Message queues introduced for inter-service communication.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Latency</h3><p>Caching added to reduce response latency.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Security</h3><p>Two-factor authentication for sensitive trading operations.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section case-split page-shell">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING JUDGMENT</span><h2>Reliability and security belong in the request path.</h2></div>
    <div class="case-notes">
      <article><h3>Asynchronous boundaries</h3><p>Message queues were used where reliable communication between services mattered.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Latency-conscious access</h3><p>Caching reduced response latency; the unsupported numerical estimate is deliberately omitted.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Sensitive actions</h3><p>Two-factor authentication strengthened operations such as buying or selling assets.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence-boundary-panel page-shell">
    <span class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE BOUNDARY</span>
    <h2>What this case study does not claim.</h2>
    <p>No proprietary code, production topology, client data, traffic volume, internal implementation detail, or performance metric is published. The work is described at the highest level approved by the portfolio owner.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
